# The upstream Swiss commit Indigo is built on.
#
# Every file outside Indigo's own paths (the interface; see OWN in
# buildtools/ci/check_upstream.py) matches this commit, line endings aside,
# except the paths listed below: Indigo's own changes to upstream files, each
# with the reason. A path ending in / covers its directory. CI checks it both
# ways: an unlisted change fails, and so does a line that no longer applies.
#
# Changing an upstream file: list it here, with why, in the same pull request.
# Moving to another upstream commit: buildtools/upstream_merge.sh <commit>, in
# a pull request of its own.

upstream https://github.com/emukidid/swiss-gc.git
commit abe21df5165e9cfe8cdbb908f9f44e137fcfae98 (Swiss master, 2026-10-22 intake)

Makefile                                   make dev also builds the packer, for In-Game Reset's apploader.img; verifies and extracts the pinned libiconv-lite overlay before compiling
cube/packer/Makefile                       compresses with xz: the build image has no 7z; links its files in byte order, whatever the locale
cube/swiss/Makefile                        tags.h is empty (its reader, load_auto_dol, never runs in Indigo); links its files in byte order, names the commit in exactly 7 characters and no build path, so the DOL is the same in any locale, clone and folder; UI_PERF=1 builds the performance overlay; no unwind tables, which nothing reads; AESND is built from cube/swiss/aesnd, not -laesnd; libiconv-lite overlay precedes the SDK portlibs; the Settings menu-action controller uses -Os while renderers and loaders keep -O2
cube/swiss/aesnd/                          libogc2's AESND at the toolchain's commit, including its upstream AESND_Reset fix (its README.md)
cube/swiss/include/gcm.h                   adjust_tgc_fst takes the file table's size
cube/swiss/source/devices/deviceHandler.c  devices shut down on reset after the interface stops reading them (priority 1)
cube/swiss/source/devices/memcard/deviceHandler-CARD.c  save reads and erases keep their exact game and maker codes; copied headers cannot use libogc2's wildcard codes; each slot's mounts are counted, so Memory Cards deletes a failed copy only on the card it wrote to
cube/swiss/source/devices/memcard/deviceHandler-CARD.h  declares that mount count (card_mount_count)
cube/swiss/source/bba.c                    once the network is up, its thread starts Sync Clock (Settings › Network, gui/time_sync.c), which sets the clock from an NTP server on a thread of its own; init_network() waits for it, so a network device never has the clock stepped under its timeouts
cube/swiss/source/gcm.c                    every walk of a file table stays inside it (fst_entries, fst_name): a damaged image cannot crash the Library, a launch or a disc opened as a folder
cube/swiss/source/devices/filemeta.c       evicted metadata returns to meta_mspace, eviction stops if every entry is in view, 7-bit ASCII banner text skips uchardet/iconv, and TGC metadata populates diskId
cube/swiss/source/video.c                  the retrace callback scans the pads through padsScan(), which the menus read; first setVideoMode resets VI_DCR before VIDEO_Init and skips GX_AbortFrame before GX_Init so warm-booted DOLs do not hang in VIDEO_WaitForFlush
cube/swiss/source/util.c                   print_debug also keeps each line for the console lab's log and LogHost (gui/lab.c), stamped with the time since the first line
cube/swiss/source/fatfs/ffunicode.c        the DBCS code-page tables are removed; code page 437 never compiles them
cube/swiss/source/nkit.c                   Latin-1 bytes in game titles are written as \x escapes; the same bytes compile
cube/swiss/source/littlefs/                vendored as files, at the commit upstream's submodule names
.gitmodules                                no submodule: littlefs is vendored
cube/swiss/source/resources/               design sources and Windows tools the build never uses are not carried
cube/swiss/source/aram/sidestep.c           retain the r2482 shutdown handoff: __SYS_InitTime is not exported by the pinned libogc2 SDK; the newer-SDK reset call from 99b59e7a is deferred
